Apply after 0001, from the ztOS checkout's `ztmetro/` directory, with GNU
`patch` (the diff paths are relative to that directory, as in the local camera
kit); the header above is skipped by patch:

    cd ztmetro
    patch -p1 -F0 < ../patches/userspace/ztcamera/0004-pacer-retime.patch

Effect: the encoder writes to <path>.part; when recording stops, the
container timeline is retimed to the wall clock with an `-itsscale` stream copy
(no frame added, dropped or re-encoded), then renamed into place. On any
failure the old behaviour is kept, so a clip is never lost. This removes the
1.4-1.7x speed-up; it does not raise the unique-frame ceiling.

Status: candidate, not accepted state. Host-verified: rebased onto the live
application line and applies with -F0 without fuzz or offset; the diff body is
identical to the original pacer diff. Offline check on real clips: 6.533 s of
file retimed to 10.632 s against 10.633 s of wall clock, 196/196 frames, decode
rc=0. The pacer candidate build (vblank + AF + retime) was built twice
byte-identically and passed the artifact check host-side; it was never run on
the phone and is not installed.

